The project memory settings are likely not configured or are configured to an insufficient value.
The daemon will restart for the next build, which may increase subsequent build times.
These settings can be adjusted by setting 'org.gradle.jvmargs' in 'gradle.properties'.
The currently configured max heap space is '2 GiB' and the configured max metaspace is '512 MiB'.
For more information on how to set these values, please refer to https://docs.gradle.org/9.0.0/userguide/build_environment.html#sec:configuring_jvm_memory in the Gradle documentation.
To disable this warning, set 'org.gradle.daemon.performance.disable-logging=true'.
